fixture        receiver                BITCASTs  nodes
narrow-e4m3    f2f_dt[fr] (4-arg)             2     56
narrow-e4m3    v.cast(fr) (3-arg)             1     56
narrow-e5m2    f2f_dt[fr] (4-arg)             2     57
narrow-e5m2    v.cast(fr) (3-arg)             1     57
narrow-fnuz    f2f_dt[fr] (4-arg)             2     51
narrow-fnuz    v.cast(fr) (3-arg)             1     51
wide-f64       f2f_dt[fr] (4-arg)             1     28
wide-f64       v.cast(fr) (3-arg)             1     29


READ IT AS: 2 BITCASTs on a narrowing pair = the incoming `v.bitcast(fr)` was
NOT folded (dtype.py's own receiver is a uint). 1 BITCAST = the incoming one
folded. The NARROWING rows are the ones item 3 is about. `f2f_dt[fr]` is the receiver
dtype.py's own two call sites pass; the 3-arg row is what `f2f-padoracle.py` and
`dd-bandpad.bend` build. A fold that only happens in the 3-arg row is a FIXTURE
difference, and landing `dd_bcast` for it would delete a node CPython builds.
